    <DataNode elementId="CPD-506" textLabel="D-myo-inositol (1,3,4,5)-tetrakisphosphate" type="Metabolite">
      <Xref identifier="CIPFCGZLFXVXBG-CNWJWELYSA-F" dataSource="InChIKey" />
      <Graphics centerX="1080.492431640625" centerY="844.4578247070312" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="3955e7" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="3955e7" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="xue, PMN, nilo-poyanco, SRI, caspi">|FRAME: CPD-506| can greatly influence the overall cellular |FRAME: CA+2| response by promoting |FRAME: CA+2| entry into cells. This action is mediated by GAP1&lt;sup&gt;IP4BP&lt;/sup&gt;, a GTPase-activating receptor that is located in the plasma membrane |CITS:[8141791][7843408][7729520][9388588][9560326]|.</Comment>
